Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:17:52 +0000

Every revision of a series stays on the list, so the older versions
crowd out the one under review. A reader cannot tell which thread is
current without opening them.

A revised cover letter already names the version it replaces on its
"Link to vN" line, as b4 writes it and lab-process-mail requires.
Deriving a superseded tag from that line marks the old thread with
no extra mail, and the tag comes back when the database is rebuilt.

Whole threads are tagged, since a review of an old version is as
stale as the patches it answers.
---
change-id: lryuluqwzlslormkkpoysqssstoqroyu

This is the automatic half of superseded tracking, and nothing else.
It tags the whole thread that a revised series names on its "Link to
vN: id:<message-id>" line. Nothing is hidden; filter old threads out
with "not tag:superseded". The patch applies to b/dev@upstream on its
own, and once it is applied one "notmuch new" tags the old threads,
since post-new already runs mail-tag.sh.

I ran the hook from this commit against a copy of the notmuch
database. It tags 27 threads, 136 messages, every one an older
version of a series, and a second run tags the same set.

